  "id": "veni-emmanuel",
  "name": "Veni Emmanuel",
  "source": "Fifteenth-century French processional melody, adapted by Thomas Helmore for The Hymnal Noted, Part II, 1854, and there set to J. M. Neale's translation of the Veni, veni, Emmanuel antiphons. Melody transcribed from the ABC setting in Paul Hardy's Xmas Tunebook (pghardy.net), which carries it in E minor, and checked against the Hymnary incipit for VENI EMMANUEL, 13555 46543 45313, which it matches note for note. Public domain: the fifteenth-century melody only -- nothing of any modern setting's harmony, chord symbols or arrangement is carried over, and the incipit is the independent confirmation of the note order. Arranged with no percussion track at all, as the two plainsong tunes in this songbook are: melody, a pedal fifth, and a bass that moves once a phrase.",
